# No Git LFS: GitHub release archives (and so the Zenodo snapshot) contain LFS
# pointer stubs, not the data. Large inputs are either gzipped under GitHub's
# 100 MB limit (quant_DIANN_outputs/*.csv.gz) or live on PRIDE (DIA-NN reports).

# Binary artifacts: no textual diff, no line merges, no line-ending rewriting.
# SVG is deliberately excluded — it is XML, and readable diffs are worth keeping there.
*.pdf binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.gz  binary

# Source files: stored LF in the repository and checked out LF, regardless of
# core.autocrlf. Without this, a CRLF blob plus core.autocrlf=true means the
# first edit to a file rewrites every line as a spurious whitespace diff.
# Data artifacts (*.csv, *.svg, *.txt) are deliberately left alone so this rule
# does not renormalize ~1100 generated files.
*.R        text eol=lf
*.Rmd      text eol=lf
*.md       text eol=lf
*.Rprofile text eol=lf
*.ps1      text eol=crlf
